## Key points

- **Conditional rendering**: `{hasMore && <button>...</button>}` — the button only appears when `hasMore` is `true`.
- **Determining `hasMore`**: Common approaches, pick based on your API:
  - Fewer items returned than the page size (`results.length < PAGE_SIZE`)
  - An explicit flag from the API (e.g., `data.hasNextPage`)
  - Comparing total count: `items.length < data.total`
- **Loading state**: Disables the button and shows feedback so users can't double-click during a fetch.

If you'd prefer, you can also disable the button instead of hiding it — just swap the conditional for `disabled={!hasMore || loading}`.

