## Key points

- **Conditional rendering**: The badge is only rendered when `originalPrice > price`. If `originalPrice` is missing, `null`, or equal to/lower than `price`, nothing renders.
- **Defensive check**: `originalPrice && originalPrice > price` handles `undefined`/`null` safely.
- **Bonus**: I also show a discount percentage and a strike-through original price — both gated by the same `isOnSale` flag, so they stay in sync.
- **Accessibility**: `aria-label="On sale"` helps screen readers announce the badge meaningfully.

If you'd prefer a boolean `isOnSale` prop instead of inferring from prices, you can swap the check to `const isOnSale = product.isOnSale;` — but deriving it from the data avoids inconsistency between the flag and the actual prices.

Here's a self-contained `ProductCard` component that renders a "Sale" badge only when an actual discount exists.

```jsx
import React from "react";
import "./ProductCard.css";

const currencyFormatter = (currency) =>
  new Intl.NumberFormat("en-US", { style: "currency", currency });

export default function ProductCard({
  name,
  image,
  price,
  originalPrice,
  currency = "USD",
  onAddToCart,
}) {
  // A sale exists only if we have a real original price that is higher.
  const hasDiscount =
    typeof originalPrice === "number" &&
    Number.isFinite(originalPrice) &&
    originalPrice > price;

  const discountPercent = hasDiscount
    ? Math.round(((originalPrice - price) / originalPrice) * 100)
    : 0;

  const format = currencyFormatter(currency);

  return (
    <article className="product-card">
      <div className="product-card__media">
        <img className="product-card__image" src={image} alt={name} />

        {hasDiscount && (
          <span className="product-card__badge">
            Sale
            {discountPercent > 0 && (
              <span className="product-card__badge-pct"> −{discountPercent}%</span>
            )}
          </span>
        )}
      </div>

      <div className="product-card__body">
        <h3 className="product-card__title">{name}</h3>

        <p className="product-card__price">
          <span className="product-card__price-current">{format.format(price)}</span>

          {hasDiscount && (
            <>
              <s className="product-card__price-original">
                {format.format(originalPrice)}
              </s>
              <span className="visually-hidden">
                , reduced from {format.format(originalPrice)}
              </span>
            </>
          )}
        </p>

        {onAddToCart && (
          <button
            type="button"
            className="product-card__cta"
            onClick={() => onAddToCart({ name, price })}
          >
            Add to cart
          </button>
        )}
      </div>
    </article>
  );
}
```

