Here's a clean, reusable implementation:

```tsx
// ErrorBanner.tsx
import { useEffect, useState } from "react";

type ErrorBannerProps = {
  /** The error message. When null/undefined/empty, nothing is rendered. */
  message?: string | null;
  /** Optional callback fired when the user dismisses the banner. */
  onDismiss?: () => void;
  /** Optional heading shown above the message. */
  title?: string;
};

export function ErrorBanner({ message, onDismiss, title = "Something went wrong" }: ErrorBannerProps) {
  const [visible, setVisible] = useState(Boolean(message));

  // Reset visibility whenever a new message arrives (or the error clears).
  useEffect(() => {
    setVisible(Boolean(message));
  }, [message]);

  // Nothing to show → render nothing at all.
  if (!message || !visible) return null;

  return (
    <div role="alert" aria-live="assertive" className="error-banner">
      <div className="error-banner__content">
        <strong className="error-banner__title">{title}</strong>
        <p className="error-banner__message">{message}</p>
      </div>

      {onDismiss && (
        <button
          type="button"
          className="error-banner__dismiss"
          aria-label="Dismiss error"
          onClick={() => {
            setVisible(false);
            onDismiss();
          }}
        >
          ×
        </button>
      )}
    </div>
  );
}
```

Usage:

```tsx
function ProfileForm() {
  const [error, setError] = useState<string | null>(null);

  async function save() {
    try {
      await api.saveProfile();
      setError(null);
    } catch (err) {
      setError(err instanceof Error ? err.message : "Unable to save profile");
    }
  }

  return (
    <>
      <ErrorBanner message={error} onDismiss={() => setError(null)} />
      <button onClick={save}>Save</button>
    </>
  );
}
```

A few notes:

- **Conditional rendering**: returning `null` means the banner adds no DOM node at all when there's no error — no empty margins, no layout shift.
- **Accessibility**: `role="alert"` + `aria-live="assertive"` makes screen readers announce the error as soon as it appears.
- **Dismissal**: the local `visible` state lets the user close the banner without the parent having to clear the error immediately; the `useEffect` re-syncs it if a new error arrives later.

